{
  "type": "Collection",
  "id": "drought-hazard",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "Extreme value return levels of the 6-month Standardised Precipitation Evapotranspiration Index (SPEI-6), modelled per grid cell from the [CSIC Global SPEI Database](https://spei.csic.es/spei_database/) for January 1902 to December 2018 with Poisson-Generalized Pareto point process models. Each item is one SPEI threshold (-1.0, -1.5, -2.0, -2.5, -3.0) and holds six cloud-optimized GeoTIFFs, one per return period: 25, 50, 100, 250, 500, and 1000 years. A pixel is the number of months with SPEI at or below the threshold for that return period. Higher values mean more severe drought. The model resolution is about 0.5°. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for access patterns.",
